                  <provenance>Written for use in the diocese of Lincoln (?). In the calendar are some saints venerated in the Low Countries, the names
                     of some English saints are wrongly spelt (fols. 50v-51); St. Rumwold is at Nov. 3 in the calendar and st. Wallepaxtus martyr in the litany..</provenance>
                  <provenance>Extensively annotated in the 16th century in English and Latin, adding
                     rubrics, running heads, psalm numbers, and additional prayers.</provenance>
                  <provenance>On fol. 11v are the names of <persName role="sgn">Raphe Faukener</persName> and Thomas (16th century).</provenance>
                  <acquisition> Part of the liturgical collection created by H. O. Coxe <foreign>c.</foreign> 1877; one of the thirty-five manuscripts of unknown provenance which retains the MS. Liturg. shelfmark (Summary Catalogue 5:843-4), several of which may belong to the Rawlinson collection. </acquisition>
               </history>
